Subject: [PATCH 26/30] =?UTF-8?q?BlueOS:=20SystemUI:=20lock=20text=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=C2=AB=D0=92=D1=81=D0=B5=D0=B3=D0=B4=D0=B0=20=D1=81=D0=B2=D0=B5?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=D1=82=D0=BB=D1=8B=D0=B9=C2=BB,=20the=20clock=20asks=20the=20sy?=
 =?UTF-8?q?stem=20for=20the=20theme?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In the light theme the clock's digits stayed light while the greeting and the date went dark: the clock read the
theme from its context, which kept saying «dark» after a switch to the light theme; the greeting read the system's
configuration. Both read the system's configuration now and decide the same way.
«Цвет текста на блокировке» gets «Всегда светлый» (the default): clock, halo, greeting and date light in both
themes on any wallpaper.

Change-Id: Iec7852bf5549eeb9b9ec54fc4a7aa7dbaabf1508
---
 .../android/keyguard/ClockEventController.kt    | 17 +++++++++++------
 .../keyguard/KeyguardSliceViewController.java   | 14 ++++++++------
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/keyguard/ClockEventController.kt b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/keyguard/ClockEventController.kt
index 99a1fb61cca0..6a56222ffd10 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/keyguard/ClockEventController.kt
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/keyguard/ClockEventController.kt
@@ -268,12 +268,17 @@ constructor(
 
     private fun updateColors() {
         val isDarkTheme = isDarkTheme()
-        // BlueOS 0.7.2: «Цвет текста на блокировке» — «По теме» (default): the dark theme keeps the clock (and its
-        // halo) light like stock Android, only the light theme follows the wallpaper under the clock; «По обоям»:
-        // always the wallpaper (0.5–0.7.1: a light wallpaper made everything dark even in the dark theme)
-        if (regionSamplingEnabled && isDarkTheme &&
-            org.blueos.arona.BlueOSSettings.int(context.contentResolver,
-                org.blueos.arona.BlueOSSettings.LOCK_TEXT_COLOR) == 0) {
+        // BlueOS 0.7.2: «Цвет текста на блокировке» — «Всегда светлый» (default): the clock (and its halo) light on
+        // any wallpaper in both themes; «По теме»: the dark theme keeps it light like stock Android, only the light
+        // theme follows the wallpaper under the clock; «По обоям»: always the wallpaper (0.5–0.7.1: a light wallpaper
+        // made everything dark even in the dark theme). The theme comes from the system's configuration, like the
+        // greeting's (KeyguardSliceViewController): this context's theme kept saying «dark» after a switch to the
+        // light theme (measured: light digits over a dark greeting).
+        val textColor = org.blueos.arona.BlueOSSettings.int(context.contentResolver,
+            org.blueos.arona.BlueOSSettings.LOCK_TEXT_COLOR)
+        val systemDark = (android.content.res.Resources.getSystem().configuration.uiMode and
+            android.content.res.Configuration.UI_MODE_NIGHT_MASK) == android.content.res.Configuration.UI_MODE_NIGHT_YES
+        if (regionSamplingEnabled && (textColor == 2 || (textColor == 0 && systemDark))) {
             clock?.run {
                 smallClock.updateTheme { it.copy(isDarkTheme = true) }
                 largeClock.updateTheme { it.copy(isDarkTheme = true) }
diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/keyguard/KeyguardSliceViewController.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/keyguard/KeyguardSliceViewController.java
index 1d173ffb6191..37fb00b5c578 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/keyguard/KeyguardSliceViewController.java
